  "term": "hypnagogic",
  "definition": "Hypnagogic refers to the transitional state around sleep, especially the half-waking condition as a person is falling asleep, waking up, or under a general anaesthetic. It can also describe experiences in that state, such as images or illusions that may shape dream content.",
